{
  "type": "final",
  "toolRequest": null,
  "final": {
    "publicNarration": {
      "beats": [
        {
          "text": "Back in the mill’s packing room, you find Hobb sweeping flour away from the bench. The machinery’s steady clatter nearly swallows your greeting, but he looks up and rests both hands on the broom.",
          "requiresOperations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "“You’re welcome. Glad to have had a careful pair of hands.” At your question, he glances toward the doorway. “Morning’s been fair. Caught up on my tallies. Been trying to sweep this floor, but every time someone opens that door, the breeze gives me the flour back.” He smiles faintly. “Not much to complain of, if that’s the worst of it.”",
          "requiresOperations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "He props the broom against the bench, willing to leave it a moment. “And yours? Had a chance to put your feet up after all that hammering?”",
          "requiresOperations": []
        }
      ],
      "visualDescription": null,
      "sceneLocale": {
        "label": "Village mill — packing room",
        "requiresOperations": []
      }
    },
    "genericOperations": [],
    "privatePatches": [],
    "publicBehavior": []
  }
}

{
  "narration": "Hobb pauses beside the packing crates, wiping flour from his palms. He glances toward the locked back-room door, then meets your eyes.\n\n“No, I keep that room private.” His voice is firm, without irritation. “Thank you for asking, though. If you’re after the packing work, there’s no need to go in there.”\n\nHe rests a hand on a crate and waits for your reply.",
  "visualDescription": "Inside the village mill, pale window light catches flour dust above rough wooden packing crates. Hobb stands beside them, facing Ari; the closed back-room door sits in shadow behind him. Grounded cinematic noir, muted colors, widescreen framing.",
  "clarification": null,
  "sceneLocale": "Village mill"
}
